  "task": {
    "objective": "Coordinate beacon control, cover, pursuit, decoy placement and rescues to capture both opposing players simultaneously.",
    "natural_termination": "The game terminates when either team has both players captured after the simultaneous capture/rescue phase. If both teams are fully captured on that step, winner remains -1 for a draw. A horizon of 128 otherwise truncates without assigning a winner.",
    "interaction": "Teammates share information, cover and rescues. Beacons give radar and consumable protection; enemy decoys suppress detection and wards and can consume a pursuer move by stunning it at a real cell. Conflicting capture intentions resolve simultaneously.",
    "observation_access": "Own-team telemetry, beacon state and capture/rescue identity notices are public to the relevant observation channels. Opponents require direct range or friendly beacon radar and may be hidden by enemy jammers. Adjacent opponents are always visible. Decoys are explicitly labeled when seen; no false indistinguishability claim is made."
